---
description: TaskHub Error-Driven Learning & Pattern Enforcement
alwaysApply: false
---
- Classify errors (compilation, runtime, pattern violation, TaskHub-specific) and analyze root cause.
- Formulate and store corrective patterns in session memory.
- Apply learned patterns proactively before generating code.
- Validate all code against TaskHub conventions and prevent regression.
- Critical patterns: Async-first backend, Zod type safety, SignalR consistency, endpoint security.
- Important: TDD compliance, performance, error boundaries.
- Preferential: File size <200 lines, naming conventions, JSDoc for complex logic.